<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Micronesia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1965–1979</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/micronesia">Micronesia</a> was the elected legislature of the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands, created in 1965 and first convened at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saipan">Saipan</a>. It became the forum in which Micronesian leaders negotiated their future political status with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The territory's districts eventually chose separate paths: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-mariana-islands">Northern Mariana Islands</a> became an American commonwealth, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federated-states-of-micronesia">Federated States of Micronesia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palau">Palau</a> became self-governing states.</p></div>
